<topic xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
       xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/topic.v2.xsd"
       title="Codecov: What's new" id="Codecov-Whats-New">

    <primary-label ref="codecov"/>
    <show-structure for="chapter" depth="2"/>

    <link-summary>Release notes for the Codecov plugin: platform support in 2026.3 and 2026.2, and the features added in 2026.1.</link-summary>
    <card-summary>Release notes for recent Codecov plugin versions.</card-summary>
    <web-summary>What's new in the Codecov plugin for JetBrains IDEs: 2026.3 platform support, the Codecov Metrics dashboard, folder coverage and coverage tools.</web-summary>

    <p>
        This page summarizes the user-facing changes in recent releases.
        For every version, see the <a href="https://plugins.jetbrains.com/plugin/23390-codecov/versions">version history on JetBrains Marketplace</a>.
    </p>

    <chapter title="Codecov 2026.3" id="platform-support">
        <p>Codecov 2026.3.1 and 2026.3.2 (September 2026) target the IntelliJ Platform 2026.3 and update dependencies.
            They add no new user features.</p>
        <p>For the supported IDE versions, see <a href="Codecov-Installation.topic" anchor="codecov-requirements"/>.</p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Codecov 2026.2" id="release-2026-2">
        <p>Codecov 2026.2.2 to 2026.2.5 (June to August 2026) target the IntelliJ Platform 2026.2 and update dependencies, including security fixes in libraries.</p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Codecov 2026.1" id="release-2026-1">
        <p>The 2026.1 releases (January to May 2026) added the dashboard and folder coverage:</p>

        <chapter title="Codecov Metrics dashboard" id="metrics-graphs">
            <p>
                The <control>Codecov Metrics</control> editor tab shows pull request impact cards and a coverage trend chart with metric, branch and time range filters.
                Open it from the Project tool window toolbar.
            </p>
            <p>
                A notification warns when a commit lowers total coverage on a branch, and the dashboard refreshes when you switch Git branches.
            </p>
            <p>For details, see <a href="Codecov-Metrics.topic"/>.</p>
        </chapter>

        <chapter title="Folder coverage" id="folder-colors">
            <p>
                Folders in the Project tool window can show a colored dot for their Codecov coverage.
                You set the coverage bands and their colors in <ui-path>Settings | Tools | Codecov | Folder Coverage</ui-path>.
            </p>
            <p>For details, see <a href="Codecov-Folder-Coverage.topic"/>.</p>
        </chapter>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Earlier versions" id="release-2025">
        <p>
            The 2025.2 releases introduced line coverage in the editor gutter with show, hide and refresh actions, the coverage popup with <control>Open in Codecov</control>, AI prompt templates, automatic repository detection from Git remotes, and support for GitHub, GitLab, Bitbucket and self-hosted Codecov servers.
            Completion and validation for <path>codecov.yml</path> have been available since the first version.
        </p>
    </chapter>

